  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/geometry/src/geometry/feature/g1_seam.rs` (new): the G1 seam rule of `feature::chains`. Two feature edges join at a vertex when all of these are true:\n  - the two edges separate the same two welded patches, or both are the rim of one open sheet;\n  - the vertex has no other real feature edge (a tessellation seam inside one patch does not count);\n  - the turn is at most `CHAIN_TANGENT_DEG` (30 degrees).\n- `crates/geometry/src/geometry/feature/trail.rs` (new): the trail walk, moved out of `feature.rs`. It keeps a joined pair consecutive in one trail. With no seam pair in a component, the walk is the same as before.\n- `feature.rs` shrinks by 6 lines. It is still over the 400-line limit, as on `main`.\n- `testdata/models/fig8.step`: new fixture from the maintainer's model.\n- `docs/decisions/2209-join-g1-edges.md`: the angle limit, the layer, and the dropped options.\n\nRoot cause: `fig8.step` has 70 `EDGE_CURVE` entities, so the file does not store short edges. The face rule joins two edges only when they bound one planar face. On a crease between a cone and a cylinder, no two chords share a planar face, so each chord was one chain.\n\n## Readings (fig8.step)\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| pickable edges | 2162 | 2162 |\n| chains | 1593 | 877 |\n| runs of the edge below the chamfer (z 19) | 719, longest 17.22 mm | 10, longest 188.49 mm |\n| runs of the edge above the chamfer (z 20) | 10, longest 194.77 mm | 10, longest 194.77 mm |\n\nOver all STEP fixtures in `testdata/models`, the tangent pieces at a two-edge vertex were: fig8 719 and spline_revolved 59 before. After the fix, the count is 0 in each fixture.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/feature_edge_g1_join.rs`:\n- `fig8_edge_below_the_chamfer_picks_whole_like_the_edge_above`\n- `no_pickable_edge_is_a_tangent_piece_of_a_longer_one_in_any_step_fixture`\n- `a_smooth_crease_cut_into_chords_chains_as_one_edge`\n- `a_sharp_corner_on_the_same_crease_still_splits`\n- `a_degenerate_band_never_panics`\n\nGate (debug, `-j 6`): all `camcraft-geometry` suites pass. These `camcraft-app` suites pass: `feature`, `feature_pick`, `feature_pick_wire`, `feature_edge_g1_join`, `pick`, `pick_agnostic`, `area_chains`, `area_picks`, `area_open`, `box_pick`, `golden_cl`, `slot_picks`, `opframe_picks`, `contour_start_point`, `heights_selection`, `project_roundtrip`, `mcp_pick`, `plane_align_edges`, `vertex_pick`, `circular_pick`, `regression_models`, `deburr_links`. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Saved selections and goldens\n\n- No golden `.cl` or `.nc` file changed. `golden_cl` passes without an update.\n- A saved chain selection that holds the id of one old piece still resolves. `feature::resolve_chain` falls back from chain to run to the single edge id. The old id is the id of that one chord, so it resolves to the same chord. It never resolves to a different edge.\n- A chain that now holds more chords gets a new chain id. A new pick of that edge selects the full edge.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full quick gate (it runs all downstream suites of `camcraft-geometry`). Only the suites above ran.\n- The ui suites, and the GUI by hand. A release build is given to the maintainer for a hand test.\n- Frame time while an edge is selected (#2201). It was not measured.\n\nChangelog: An edge between two curved faces (for example below a chamfer on a round wall) now picks as one full edge, not as many short pieces.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2209\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
